# Toyota Yaris XP90 five-door hatchback, 2006-2011.
#
# The second-generation Yaris. Toyota GB put it on sale on 1 January 2006; the
# Toyota GB timeline gives June 2006, and both dates are recorded because the
# two Toyota GB sources conflict. Launched at £8,995 for the 1.0 VVT-i T2
# three-door and £13,295 for the 1.4 D-4D T Spirit five-door with MultiMode,
# on the road. Replaced in August 2011 by the XP130.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Gen2-Yaris-archive-press-pack.pdf
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Yaris-archive-timeline.pdf
#
# Dimensions 3.750 x 1.695 x 1.520 m, wheelbase 2.460 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Vitz", second-generation XP90 infobox: wheelbase
# 2,460 mm, length 3,750 mm for 2005-2008 and 3,785 mm for 2008-2010, width
# 1,695 mm, height 1,520 mm for front-wheel drive. The pre-facelift car is
# modelled. The hull measures 3.750 m on a 2.460 m wheelbase, 65.6 per cent;
# the assembled model is 3.810 m long once the number plates are included, and
# 1.936 m wide over the mirrors.
#
# Shape reference: the pack holds one rear-left three-quarter of a yellow
# three-door and three views of black and white five-doors. The five-door is
# the body modelled; the three-door image was used only for the roof line and
# the tail, and its roof bars were not modelled. No true side elevation exists,
# so the flank was built from the photographs with the wheel centres fixed by
# the published ratio.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB brochure names, evidence grade (a): the 2009 brochure
# lists Cirrus White, Crystal Silver, Venetian Silver, Alsace Granite, Eclipse
# Black, Decuma Grey, Chilli Red, Carlo Blue and Vivid Blue; the 2010 brochure
# repeats most of them. Four common British finishes are modelled: Crystal
# Silver, Cirrus White, Eclipse Black and Chilli Red. Weights silver 3, white
# 3, red 2, black 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 170 km/h, the 1.3-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 80/450, on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 80: roomier and better insulated than the XP10. Classes
# 1,2, the mainstream small hatchback bands of the 2000s.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 2006 intro, retires staggered 2018-2021 on a
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp90.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp90.dae (42 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-yaris-xp90/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is flatter than the photographs and the
# headlamps do not wrap round the front corners far enough; the wheel arch
# transitions are abrupt, the door cuts incomplete and the shoulder crease weak;
# the wheel covers are simplified. The top view confirms a continuous painted
# roof and the windscreen is visible from the front. At 128 px the tall domed
# body, the short overhangs and the vertical tail lamps read as the XP90.

